      "widgets_values": [
        "[IDENTITY RULES — keep for every stage]\nAll three reference photos show the SAME real adult man. Use the front photo <image1> as the primary identity reference; <image2> and <image3> only clarify the same face from the sides. Preserve his actual recognizable face, natural facial proportions, eyes, nose, mouth, skin tone, hairline and short haircut. Do not average him into a new generic model. Keep natural skin detail, asymmetry and a realistic adult appearance; no beauty-filter face, no enlarged eyes, no cartoon features. One person, one single photo, no collage, no text, no watermark.\n\n[STAGE A — frontal half-body identity candidate]\nCreate a natural photorealistic frontal half-body instructor portrait of this same 27-year-old man, framed from the head to just below the waist, looking at the camera. A composed, calm face with a very subtle closed-mouth friendly smile. Keep the short haircut and recognizable hairline, simply tidy the loose strands. The only intentional facial accessory change is replacing the existing dark-rimmed glasses with thin rimless prescription glasses, transparent lenses, small subtle metal bridge and temples. Preserve the actual eyes and their size; do not stylize or enlarge them. Simple contemporary black crew-neck T-shirt with a lightweight plain dark overshirt, no logos, natural lightly muscular build, relaxed upright posture. Soft even light, plain warm light-gray studio background, realistic skin texture. Young and composed with understated playful warmth. Keep the real face as the priority over fashion or retouching. This is an identity candidate for owner review, not an already-approved baseline.",
